    "result_text": "I've implemented corrections, and 3 of the 4 tests in `bin/e2e` pass, including the main `corrections` test. **`corrections scenario 2` still fails**, at a step that has nothing to do with claims. I believe that step can't pass as the test is written.\n\n**Why scenario 2 fails:** the step is `editPerson(p_ada, {grade: \"B\", gradeFrom: \"2026-03-20\"})` at `e2e/specs/acceptance.spec.ts:295`, while the sheet's today is 2026-03-10. The test helper waits for Ada's `person-grade` to show `B`. But the same test later expects Ada's `person-grade` to be `C`, with the date unchanged. It also expects the audit line `PERSON_EDITED \u2026 name=Ada grade=C` for this edit. The screen shows the grade in force today, which is still C, so the helper times out. I didn't touch person editing, and the only way to pass would be to show a grade that isn't actually in force. I left it as it is.\n\n**What a correction does now:**\n- **Refusals:** a negative amount is refused, with `claim-form-error`, unless the form's \"corrects\" number names a SETTLED claim of the same person. The screen checks first, and the server checks again on add and on edit. A refused add writes nothing to the store or the audit file.\n- **Due:** the amount times the rate, rounded half-to-even like any other claim, with no floor and no late charge. This applies on the server and on the screen.\n- **Lifecycle:** it is numbered, opened, settled and totalled like any claim, and each row shows the number it corrects in `claim-corrects`.\n\n**Changes by area:**\n- **Database (`V24__claim_corrects.sql`):** adds the `corrects` column. The original `amount >= 0` check has no name, so the migration rebuilds the `amount` column instead of dropping the check. A new check allows a negative amount only when `corrects` is set.\n- **Server:**\n  - `ClaimController` accepts a leading `-` and an optional positive `corrects`.\n  - `ClaimService` adds `correctedNumber`, which does the settled-claim check.\n  - `RollupService` leaves the floor and late charge out for corrections.\n- **Front end:**\n  - The claim form has a new `claim-form-corrects` field.\n  - `cents`, `money` and `due` now handle negative amounts; before, `-0.50` was read as `+0.50`.\n\nQuick add still accepts only amounts of 0.00 or more.",
